course: dictionary
lesson: 11782
title: A famous name in music
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Beethoven is a name. It belongs to a person, so it starts with a capital letter. When you meet a name you don't know, ask: is this a person, a place, or a thing? The words around it will give you the clue.
explain: «Beethoven wrote music even after he became deaf.» The word «wrote» tells you Beethoven made something, and «music» tells you what it was. So Beethoven must be a person who writes music, a composer.
explain: You may hear his music in class, such as «Für Elise» or the «Ode to Joy». When you hear the name in a sentence, swap in your meaning and check it still makes sense: «Mozart wrote music even after he became deaf» would be wrong, because the story is about Beethoven.
fact: Beethoven is a proper noun, which is the name of a particular person, so it begins with a capital letter.
fact: Ludwig van Beethoven (1770–1827) was a German composer, one of the most famous in history.
fact: Beethoven kept writing music even after he became deaf.
fact: His famous works include the Fifth Symphony, which goes da-da-da-DUM, and «Für Elise».
fact: His story is often told as an example of not giving up.
exercise: «Beethoven wrote music even after he became deaf.» Who is Beethoven in this sentence? | A school teacher | *A German composer, a person who writes music | A kind of drum | A town in the hills
exercise: In music class we played «Für Elise» by Beethoven. What is «Für Elise»? | *A piece of music by Beethoven | A type of instrument | A German city | A name of a school
exercise: Which word is a name, so it needs a capital letter? | symphony | composer | *Beethoven | music
test: The Fifth Symphony starts with a famous rhythm. What is it? | hum-hum-hum | la-la-la-la | *da-da-da-DUM | ding-ding-ding
test: Why is Beethoven's story told in lessons? | Because he was a famous footballer | *Because he did not give up, even when he could not hear | Because he stopped writing music at a young age | Because he moved to the moon
exam: «Beethoven was a German composer who kept writing music after he became deaf.» What does this sentence tell you about Beethoven? | A place in Germany | *A person who wrote music, even when he was deaf | A kind of food | A dog in a family film
